<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Yemeni Socialist Party</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1978–present</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as YSP</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Yemeni Socialist Party was founded in October 1978 when <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-yemen">South Yemen</a>'s ruling <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/national-liberation-front-south-yemen">National Liberation Front</a> merged with smaller leftist groups. Organised on the Soviet model, it was the sole legal party of the People's <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/democratic-republic-of-yemen">Democratic Republic of Yemen</a> until unification in 1990, when it shared power with the northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/general-peoples-congress">General People's Congress</a>. Its defeat in the civil war of 1994 ended its role in government, though it survives as an opposition party.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/yemeni-socialist-party.jpg" alt="Yemeni Socialist Party" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Yemeni Socialist Party · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_Yemeni_Socialist_Party.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
